subproblems.statement:
Let P, Q, j ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P be open, V ⊆ ℝ^Q and A ⊆ U, and let f : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q be of class C^∞ with f⁻¹(K) ∩ A compact for every compact K ⊆ V. Then for every ω ∈ D^j(V) there are η ∈ D^j(U), ζ : ℝ^P → ℝ and an open set N ⊆ ℝ^P such that:
- A ⊆ N and 0 ≤ ζ ≤ 1;
- η(x) = ζ(x)·(f^#ω)(x) for all x, and η(x) = (f^#ω)(x) for all x ∈ N;
- tsupport η ⊆ f⁻¹(tsupport ω).
Here (f^#ω)(x) := ω(f(x)).compContinuousLinearMap (Df(x)).

Assume LipschitzPushforwardIntegerMultiplicity and the statement (SPF) of iwl_smooth_pushforward (exact frozen Lean type, as an antecedent). Let P, Q, m ∈ ℕ. Let U ⊆ ℝ^P and V ⊆ ℝ^Q be open, and let F ⊆ ℝ^P be any set. Let p : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q be a continuous linear map with operator norm ‖p‖ ≤ 1 and p(U) ⊆ V, such that for every compact K ⊆ V the set p⁻¹(K) ∩ F is compact and contained in U. Let X_k ∈ D_{m+1}(U) (k ∈ ℕ) be integer multiplicity currents with spt X_k ⊆ F. Then there are integer multiplicity currents S_k ∈ D_{m+1}(V) (k ∈ ℕ) such that:
(i) S_k(ω) = X_k(η) for every k, every ω ∈ D^{m+1}(V) and every η ∈ D^{m+1}(U) for which there is an open N ⊇ spt X_k with η(x) = (ω(p x)).compContinuousLinearMap p for all x ∈ N;
(ii) M_W(S_k) ≤ M(X_k) and M_W(∂S_k) ≤ M(∂X_k) for every k and every W ⊆ ℝ^Q, where M(X_k) = M_U(X_k) and M(∂X_k) = M_U(∂X_k).
